/* rnl-std-no-labels 0.3, a package of the standard series 0.3 (16.3).
   Generated by build-std.mjs in rnl-dev (notes/analog-canvas-rnl-import-export/std-0.3, 609ab05)
   from Analog Canvas 9bbfd340b (packages/components/definitions), symbol-list.json (rnl-dev f0c23b6)
   and the hand-written parts there; from here on edited in rnl, whose files are the source.
   Turns the default labels of the standard symbols off, for a file that writes its own (16.3).
   Optional, in no collection: a file names it with USE-PACKAGE. */
@RNL(type="header") { @VERSION("0.3"); @PACKAGE(name="rnl-std-no-labels", version="0.3")}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- rnl-std-no-labels: no default labels
   Not implicit. A file whose labels are all its own, such as one an editor writes, names it with
   USE-PACKAGE in its header. Every label the standard symbols give an instance or a usage (name,
   value, model) becomes empty; the file's own TEXT with the same key comes later and shows it again
   (13.3). A usage drawn with a device's symbol, such as a $FIGURE with $RESISTOR, has no value or
   model to show, and its label would fail (13.6); empty, it reads nothing. A block's formula stays:
   it is part of the drawing. A symbol without one of these keys gets an empty label for it, which
   draws nothing. */
@RNL {
  # @SELECT-INSTANCE => @TEXT("", key="name");
  # @SELECT-INSTANCE => @TEXT("", key="value");
  # @SELECT-INSTANCE => @TEXT("", key="model");
  # @SELECT-USAGE => @TEXT("", key="name");
  # @SELECT-USAGE => @TEXT("", key="value");
  # @SELECT-USAGE => @TEXT("", key="model")
}
